{
  "recipe": {
    "model_providers": [
      {
        "name": "Local Model",
        "endpoint": "",
        "provider_type": "openai",
        "extra_headers": {},
        "extra_body": {},
        "is_local": true
      }
    ],
    "mcp_providers": [],
    "model_configs": [
      {
        "alias": "problem-writer",
        "model": "unsloth/gemma-4-E2B-it-GGUF",
        "provider": "Local Model",
        "inference_parameters": {
          "temperature": 0.9,
          "max_tokens": 250
        }
      },
      {
        "alias": "solver",
        "model": "unsloth/gemma-4-E2B-it-GGUF",
        "provider": "Local Model",
        "inference_parameters": {
          "temperature": 0.3,
          "max_tokens": 700
        }
      }
    ],
    "tool_configs": [],
    "columns": [
      {
        "column_type": "sampler",
        "name": "subject",
        "drop": false,
        "sampler_type": "category",
        "params": {
          "values": [
            "arithmetic word problem",
            "unit conversion",
            "logic puzzle",
            "probability",
            "percentages and discounts",
            "time and scheduling"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "column_type": "sampler",
        "name": "difficulty",
        "drop": false,
        "sampler_type": "category",
        "params": {
          "values": [
            "easy",
            "medium"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "column_type": "sampler",
        "name": "setting",
        "drop": true,
        "sampler_type": "category",
        "params": {
          "values": [
            "a bakery",
            "a train station",
            "a school trip",
            "a community garden",
            "a sports league",
            "a small online shop",
            "a library",
            "a road trip"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "column_type": "llm-text",
        "name": "problem",
        "drop": false,
        "model_alias": "problem-writer",
        "prompt": "Write one {{ difficulty }} {{ subject }} set in {{ setting }}.\nRules:\n- It must have exactly one short final answer (a number, name or yes/no).\n- Include every fact needed to solve it.\n- 1 to 3 sentences.\n- Do not include the answer or any hints.\n- Output only the problem.",
        "system_prompt": "You write clear, self-contained practice problems.",
        "with_trace": "none",
        "extract_reasoning_content": false
      },
      {
        "column_type": "llm-structured",
        "name": "solution",
        "drop": false,
        "model_alias": "solver",
        "prompt": "Solve this problem. Think step by step in `reasoning`, showing each calculation, then give only the final answer in `final_answer`.\n\nProblem: {{ problem }}",
        "system_prompt": "You are a careful tutor who checks each step before answering.",
        "with_trace": "none",
        "extract_reasoning_content": false,
        "output_format": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "reasoning",
            "final_answer"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "reasoning": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Step-by-step working"
            },
            "final_answer": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Short final answer only"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "column_type": "expression",
        "name": "assistant",
        "drop": false,
        "expr": "<think>\n{{ solution.reasoning }}\n</think>\n\n{{ solution.final_answer }}",
        "dtype": "str"
      }
    ],
    "processors": []
  },
  "run": {
    "rows": 10,
    "preview": true,
    "output_formats": [
      "jsonl"
    ]
  },
  "ui": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "note_1",
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "width": 400,
        "node_type": "markdown_note",
        "name": "note_1",
        "markdown": "##### Reasoning traces\n\n1. Samplers pick a **subject**, **difficulty** and **setting**, so problems don't repeat.\n2. `problem` writes a problem with one short answer.\n3. `solution` is structured output: step-by-step `reasoning` plus a `final_answer`.\n4. `assistant` formats it as `<think>...</think>` followed by the answer, the shape most reasoning fine-tunes train on. Pair it with `problem` as the user turn.\n\nCheck the run's **Quality pass** for duplicate problems before training.",
        "note_color": "#DBEAFE",
        "note_opacity": "35"
      },
      {
        "id": "Local Model",
        "x": 720,
        "y": 0,
        "width": 400
      },
